---
// Four-quadrant operation, with the low-speed wedge where braking still costs power.
const C = { x: 300, y: 180 };
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 680 370" role="img" aria-labelledby="fq-title fq-desc">
  <title id="fq-title">The four quadrants of motor operation</title>
  <desc id="fq-desc">With speed on the horizontal axis and torque on the vertical, the two quadrants where torque and speed have the same sign are motoring: electrical power becomes mechanical. The two where they have opposite signs are generating: mechanical power flows back. A thin wedge along the torque axis inside the generating quadrants marks slow, hard braking, where winding heat exceeds the recovered power and the bus still supplies energy.</desc>
  <rect class="soft1" x={C.x} y="30" width="230" height="150" /><rect class="soft1" x="70" y={C.y} width="230" height="150" />
  <rect class="soft2" x="70" y="30" width="230" height="150" /><rect class="soft2" x={C.x} y={C.y} width="230" height="150" />
  <polygon class="f3" opacity="0.55" points={`${C.x},${C.y} ${C.x},30 ${C.x - 52},30`} />
  <polygon class="f3" opacity="0.55" points={`${C.x},${C.y} ${C.x},330 ${C.x + 52},330`} />
  <line class="axis" x1="60" y1={C.y} x2="540" y2={C.y} /><line class="axis" x1={C.x} y1="20" x2={C.x} y2="340" />
  <text x="544" y={C.y + 4} class="t-small t-muted">speed +</text><text x={C.x} y="14" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-muted">torque +</text>
  <text x="415" y="96" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-c1">Motoring</text><text x="415" y="114" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">pushing the way it moves</text>
  <text x="185" y="262" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-c1">Motoring</text><text x="185" y="280" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">same, in reverse</text>
  <text x="160" y="96" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-c2">Generating</text><text x="160" y="114" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">resisting the motion</text>
  <text x="440" y="262" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-c2">Generating</text><text x="440" y="280" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">power flows to the bus</text>
  <line class="link" x1={C.x + 30} y1="300" x2="556" y2="318" />
  <text x="562" y="308" class="t-small t-strong t-c3">Braking that</text><text x="562" y="323" class="t-small t-strong t-c3">still costs power</text>
  <text x="562" y="340" class="t-small">slow + high torque:</text><text x="562" y="355" class="t-small">heat &gt; recovered</text>
  <text x="70" y="362" class="t-small t-muted">Mechanical power = torque × speed. Its sign tells you which way energy is trying to flow.</text>
</svg>
